   its whole innerHTML replaced on every render(). This matters only for
   #videoSlot: see the big comment above ensureVideoHost() below for why —
   in short, an iframe reloads on ANY DOM move in Chromium (confirmed by
   direct testing), even a "safe"-looking one, so the video slot must be
   created once and never moved, appended-to-elsewhere, or rebuilt again.
   #headerSlot and #bodySlot hold no iframes, so they're simply
   re-rendered via innerHTML every time, same as the old single-slot
